    <section class="empire-glance" id="at-a-glance" aria-labelledby="glance-title">
      <div class="empire-glance-main"><h2 class="empire-glance-title" id="glance-title">At a glance</h2><ul><li>A <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia#boers">Boer</a> republic north of the Vaal River, founded by Voortrekkers and recognised by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia#britain">Britain</a> in the Sand River Convention of 1852.</li><li>Gold found on the Witwatersrand in 1886 made it the richest state in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia#africa">Africa</a> and created the city of Johannesburg.</li><li>Conflict with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia#britain">Britain</a> over the gold fields and the rights of foreign uitlanders led to the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia#second-boer-war">Second Boer War</a> and its end in 1902.</li></ul></div>
      <aside class="empire-dyk"><p class="empire-dyk-title">Did you know?</p><p>Pretoria was named after the Voortrekker leader <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia#andries-pretorius">Andries Pretorius</a> by his son <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia#marthinus-wessel-pretorius">Marthinus Wessel Pretorius</a>, who founded the town in 1855 and became the republic’s first president.</p></aside>
    </section>

